"auto.help.what" = "Usage checks only read status. This optional feature sends one small, randomized arithmetic request to eligible accounts to keep their 5h usage windows starting while the app runs.";
"auto.help.schedule" = "After a successful request, that account's next request is scheduled 5 hours from the request start. Only one account runs at a time, with at least 30 minutes between account starts. Missed requests after sleep or restart are staggered, not sent in a burst.";
"auto.help.cost" = "This makes a real model request and consumes Codex allowance. It is off by default. An available lightweight model is preferred, with low effort when supported; otherwise an available model or the runtime default is used. It does not add credits or force OpenAI to reset a limit; reset timing and allowance remain controlled by OpenAI.";
"auto.help.limits" = "Only connected accounts whose latest successful status includes a 5h limit are eligible. Weekly-only accounts, disconnected accounts and accounts awaiting sign-in are skipped. Failed automatic requests wait at least 30 minutes before another attempt. The app cannot guarantee that a request or token refresh will succeed.";
"auto.help.devices" = "Requests stop when this app is not running. For the same accounts, enable this feature on only one Mac to avoid duplicate model requests. Account authentication must still be completed by you.";
"auto.help.privacy" = "Automatic requests contain only an arithmetic expression. No documents are intentionally included. The bundled Codex runtime communicates with OpenAI and inherits the selected CODEX_HOME configuration; review any custom providers, MCP servers or runtime telemetry settings you have configured.";
"about.title" = "About this product";
"about.version" = "Version %@ (%@)";
"about.overview" = "Monitor multiple Codex accounts and workspaces from one menu bar panel. See both 5h and weekly remaining allowance, reset times and reset credits without switching your main login.";
"about.accounts" = "This Mac's default connection reuses its existing .codex login. Added accounts/workspaces use separate app-managed Codex homes. Names and display order are stored locally.";
"about.refresh" = "Opening the panel checks every connection. Optional 5h auto-refresh schedules lightweight arithmetic requests while the app runs, staggered across accounts. Real requests consume allowance and cannot override OpenAI's limits.";
"about.privacy" = "This app has no developer-operated account server, advertising SDK or app analytics upload. It does not send credentials or usage data to its developer. Authentication, status checks and optional model requests still require communication with OpenAI. The bundled runtime and any user-configured endpoints have their own network behavior.";
"about.opensource" = "Codex Usage is open source under the MIT License. Its bundled OpenAI Codex runtime is under Apache License 2.0. This is an independent project, not an official OpenAI product. OpenAI, ChatGPT and Codex are their owners' trademarks.";
